cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this code, please cite the associated manuscript.
title: >-
  Analysis code for "Avian flight accelerates genome evolution and shapes
  machineries for energy production"
abstract: >-
  Sister-pair comparative analysis of 42 avian sister pairs across 84 taxa and
  roughly 14,800 protein-coding genes, testing whether changes in flight
  behaviour drive molecular evolutionary rate acceleration and genome size
  evolution. Replaces the categorical flight predictor of the previous version
  with a continuous wing-loading index.
authors:
  - family-names: Duchene
    given-names: David A.
    email: david.duchene@sund.ku.dk
    affiliation: University of Copenhagen
repository-code: https://github.com/duchene/avian_flight_genomics
license: MIT
keywords:
  - molecular evolution
  - comparative genomics
  - birds
  - flight
  - genome size
